class:: JumpDiffusion
summary:: Gaussian diffusion with explicit compound-Poisson shocks and jump diagnostics
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Processes
related:: Classes/OUProcess, Classes/ShotNoise, Classes/TPoissonRand, Classes/LevyFlight, Guides/Stochastica

description::
A trajectory combining continuous Brownian wandering with occasional Gaussian-marked Poisson shocks. State remembers all previous displacement. Unlike LevyFlight, its jumps form a separate finite-rate mechanism with directly observable count and aggregate size. ShotNoise makes impacts decay toward zero; JumpDiffusion accumulates their displacement permanently. Setting jumpRate to zero leaves Brownian drift/diffusion, without OU mean reversion.

For each model interval dt, draw code::K ~ Poisson(jumpRate*dt):: and independently add code::drift*dt + diffusion*sqrt(dt)*Z::. Conditional on K, the total jump is Gaussian with mean code::K*jumpMean:: and standard deviation code::sqrt(K)*jumpStd::. One aggregate Gaussian draw replaces a loop over individual shocks. This is an exact finite-interval increment law for constant parameters, not a resolved timestamp for each within-step jump.

Expected displacement per interval is code::(drift+jumpRate*jumpMean)*dt:: and variance is code::(diffusion.squared+jumpRate*(jumpStd.squared+jumpMean.squared))*dt::. The Poisson component is uncompensated: drift does not subtract its average contribution. Source: the compound-Poisson moment derivation in Siegrist's link::https://www.randomservices.org/random/poisson/Compound.html::, combined with independent Gaussian diffusion. The existing bounded Poisson and Gaussian samplers are reused.

Raw finite double state is preserved without musical limiting; serialization saturates only beyond float range. Non-finite updates, or a Poisson mean above 100000000 per calculation, restore initial with zero jump diagnostics while keeping the runtime RNG position. This explicit numerical domain protects the uint32 count sampler and does not silently cap jumpRate. Counts above 2^24 lose integer resolution as floats. The sampler has at most 64 rejection attempts and a deterministic rounded-mean fallback. Work is bounded independently of the sampled count; no runtime allocation occurs. Abrupt shocks are not antialiased.

Vanilla link::Classes/BrownNoise:: provides audible random wandering; JumpDiffusion exposes an unbounded displacement model and separate Poisson shocks. Vanilla link::Classes/Dust:: can mark isolated impacts, while this UGen also preserves multiple shocks in one calculation through jumpCount and aggregate jumpSize.

