subsection:: See also
link::Classes/OUProcess::, link::Classes/ShotNoise::, link::Classes/TPoissonRand::, link::Classes/LevyFlight::, link::Guides/Stochastica::

classmethods::
method:: ar, kr
argument:: drift
Deterministic displacement per model second; finite, otherwise zero.
argument:: diffusion
Brownian diffusion amplitude, interpreted by magnitude. Variance contribution is diffusion squared times elapsed model time. Non-finite becomes zero.
argument:: jumpRate
Nonnegative Poisson rate per model second. Negative/non-finite becomes zero. Rate times elapsed model time must not exceed 100000000.
argument:: jumpMean
Finite mean of each individual Gaussian shock, otherwise zero.
argument:: jumpStd
Standard deviation of each shock, interpreted by magnitude. Zero gives fixed-size marks; non-finite becomes zero.
argument:: timeScale
Nonnegative model seconds per real second. .ar uses sample duration and .kr block duration. Nonpositive/non-finite values hold state and zero all jump diagnostics. Parameters are sampled each calculation.
argument:: initial
Position at construction, reset or numerical recovery. Non-finite becomes zero.
argument:: seed
Local PCG32 seed; nonzero repeats a sequence. Zero derives from the parent Synth only at construction.
argument:: reset
Rising nonpositive-to-positive edge restores initial and the original seed, clears all jump diagnostics and skips evolution. Held positive does not repeat.
returns::
Four outputs: code::[state, jumpTrig, jumpSize, jumpCount]::. jumpTrig is one when the count is positive, even if marks cancel or are zero. jumpSize is only the aggregate shock, excluding diffusion and drift. Flags and diagnostics describe one calculation, not latched events.

examples::
subsection:: Minimal wandering pitch
code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar((60 + JumpDiffusion.kr(diffusion: 1, jumpRate: 1, jumpStd: 7, seed: 72)[0]).clip(30, 96).midicps, 0, 0.07) ! 2 }.play
)
::

subsection:: Hear each structural shock
State moves the oscillator register; jumpTrig adds a short high accent. Audio-rate timing preserves short event flags and an explicit mapping bounds the audible pitch.
code::
(
{
    var model = JumpDiffusion.ar(diffusion: 1, jumpRate: 0.8, jumpStd: 7, seed: 72);
    var pitch = (60 + model[0]).clip(30, 96).midicps;
    var body = SinOsc.ar(pitch, 0, 0.065);
    var accent = SinOsc.ar(2400, 0, Decay2.ar(model[1], 0.001, 0.08) * 0.04);
    (body + accent) ! 2 * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
}.play
)
::
